; ============================================================================
; Sharp PC-1600  --  system ROM, Page 0 / Bank 0 (0000H-3FFFH), OLD revision
; ROM file: PC-1600-ROM/dumps/old/PC1600-P0-B0.BIN  (MD5 5afcc22134e106bfd63b899febe9df7c)
; Generated by tools/romdis/build.py from disasm/old/PC1600-P0-B0/PC1600-P0-B0.ann -- edit the
; .ann file, not this one.  Reassembles byte-identical with z80asm.
; ============================================================================
; OLD REVISION (PEEK #(0,&7FFF) = 130). Ported from the NEW revision's knowledge base
; with tools/romdis/annport.py and checked by hand; notes/PC1600-Old-vs-New.md lists the
; differences. Annotations of code that exists only in the NEW revision are left out.
;
; OVERVIEW
; Page 0 of bank 0 is the only ROM that is never switched out: it holds the
; RST vectors, the fixed jump table every program uses, the bank switching
; gateways, the reset/boot code and a large part of the BASIC interpreter.
; Bank 0 page 1 (P1-B0, 4000H-7FFFH) is the direct continuation of this image:
; the last routine here runs on into 4000H, and many routines below are called
; from there (and from the hidden BASIC ROM, bank 3b) directly.
;
;   0000H-0316H  RST vectors, fixed jump table, IM2 vector (0315H)
;   0317H-0934H  reset / power-on, work-area init, module scan, interrupt entry
;   0935H-0CE7H  bank switching core: EXROMCAL, BANKSET/READ/JUMP/CALL, RST 18H /
;                RST 20H, MEMORYCHK, SLOTxMAP, power off / auto power off
;   0CE8H-10ADH  BASIC boot: CHECK messages, WAKE$ strings, AUTORUN.BAS / ARUN
;   10AEH-1884H  peripherals poll, FILE dispatcher, ROM module token tables,
;                COMMADR/TOK2ASC, line and label search, logical addresses,
;                EXCOMMEXE, RAMODSET, CE-1600P wrappers
;   1885H-220AH  number <-> integer / text conversion, GETCDI, ASCBIN, STRCNV
;   220BH-2A7EH  interpreter helpers: LINSRH, ARRAYIND, SERROR, GOSUB stack,
;                PRINT formatting, jump targets (line numbers / labels)
;   2A7FH-2F42H  variables: VARADR, VARNAME, VARPEEK/POKE, VARGET/LET, VARPAR
;   2F43H-38A0H  expression evaluator (EXPRESS / EXPREX)
;   38A1H-39A1H  trampolines into P1-B0 and the hidden BASIC ROM 3b
;   39A2H-3FFFH  statement loop, errors, BREAK, BASIC interrupts, AUTO, keys
;
; CONVENTIONS
; - Addresses of BASIC data are "logical": 0000H-BFFFH map through ADTBL to
;   8000H-BFFFH of a RAM bank (see LOGADR); C000H-FFFFH is internal RAM.
; - Pointers kept in the BASIC work area are often stored high byte first with
;   bit 15 inverted (the PC-1500 / LH-5803 convention), e.g. CURTOP, SRCHADR.
; - FE00H holds the interpreter's processing pointer.
; - Error returns: CY set and the BASIC error code in A.
; - Each line: address, raw bytes, comment.  Labels Lxxxx / names without a
;   description are local branch targets.  Symbol table: notes/PC1600-P0-B0-Symbols.md.
; ============================================================================

